This adds the /spec-report skill, then runs it on its own spec. The
report is the second patch.

The skill reads a spec, judges the working copy against it using
implementation and documentation, uses history and notes only as
context, and commits a sibling report. The report gives a summary
status, conflicts and their :conflict-plan: headings, plans that can
be removed, gaps marked ready or not ready to implement, and what is
done, with evidence for every claim but the status. A sclr report.org
beside a lore.org is moved to sclr-report.org first.

The report finds the spec fully covered, and leaves two questions for
the spec, both about markdown specs:

1. How does a markdown spec mark a :conflict-plan: heading? SKILL.md
   assumes a heading whose text ends with ":conflict-plan:".
2. spec.org:19 lists REPORT--*.org and report--**.org, but the rule
   s/^spec/report/ at spec.org:20 turns SPEC--*.md into REPORT--*.md.
   The skill follows the rule.

The series needs "claude/skills/spec-report: Initial spec" (3119a70b
on b/dev), which adds the spec. It is not on trunk or the list, so it
is not included; the prerequisite-patch-id lines below cover b/dev.
Both patches add new files, so they also apply to trunk without it.

The report was written by following SKILL.md by hand. /spec-report
was not available as a command in this session, so the skill has
not yet been run as a command.

Changes in v2:
- Add SKILL.md, since the updated spec answers the questions the
  v1 report raised.
- Replace the hand-written report with the one the skill produces.
- Link to v1: id:99b6ba1b1449403336a4a47f726cfd12002037da.1791828849.git.claude@p7x.dev

